{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793313253,"nonce":"1rvVmf4eGhqCzKbZ3kvHsGnIl/U=","title":"Protect released recovered drafts during filesystem mutations","message":"Parent session recovery track: ae3a156433377383faa317d5da1f34e6eab10f9a6e0d0ab0456fc0e0277a8382\nCloud Sync authority track: 529764c1f9d8a4aa4fd6b9b203165dd4df383e332f1a4cbf110441de29bcaec2\n\nAfter a buffered restore, closing its document leaves unsaved text in private state while the disk contains the selected saved baseline. Current rename/remove guard only materialized documents: a released draft can be moved/deleted or overwritten via an alias, leaving its private graph stranded or unrecoverable. Protect file and directory mutations, including destination replacement and canonical aliases, after release and restart. Verify disk and graph before allowing clean mutations; preserve pending Save recovery. Bind new private buffer records to host-local paths, handle legacy unbound records conservatively and bound inspection work without idle polling. This is native draft protection, not stable distributed document IDs or complete filesystem/Git recovery.","files":null}]}